    "description": "This file includes statewide WaKIDS data by detailed race and detailed ethnicity from the 2025-26 school year. Data is at the state level and includes information the following student group types: all students, detailed race, and detailed ethnicity. Please review the notes below for more information. \n\nWaKIDS, the Washington Kindergarten Inventory of Developing Skills, includes an assessment that is administered during the first two months of kindergarten. Teachers observe students across six areas of development and learning; Social-Emotional, Physical, Language, Cognitive, Literacy and Math. While the only requirement for kindergarten is to be five years of age by August 31, children who demonstrate readiness in all six areas have a greater likelihood of success in kindergarten and beyond.",
